# API keys for the two sources that need one. Rename this file to keys.txt.
#
# One `name = value` a line. Nothing in this program ever prints a key, and
# keys.txt is in .gitignore so it cannot reach a repository.
#
# Only these two do anything. A key for anything else would sit here unread --
# there is no code in this program that could use it, which is why no other
# source is on the panel at all.
#
#   pexels   https://www.pexels.com/api/         photographs, free, instant
#   giphy    https://developers.giphy.com/       GIFs, free, instant
#
# GIPHY's free key is rate limited to 100 searches an hour and 1,000 a day.
# This program paces itself well inside that -- one search is a call or two,
# because a page is fifty GIFs -- but it is their limit, not ours.
#
# Leave a line commented out and that source is listed as needing a key rather
# than failing when you press Search.

# pexels =
# giphy =
